# Part A: Problem Formulation

## A1. Problem Statement
Retail investors utilizing the Public Gold platform face high cognitive fatigue and severe task friction due to visual clutter, fragmented navigation modules, and manual transaction verification methods. Specifically, users attempting to transition between digital gold savings (GAP) and physical installment management (EPP) must navigate disconnected sub-interfaces and manually upload bank transfer payment slips. This cumbersome process delays transaction fulfillment, increases user drop-offs, and reduces user trust during time-sensitive market price fluctuations.

## A2. Users and Scope

### Target Users & Stakeholders
* **Digital Gold Investors (GAP Users):** Require real-time spot price tracking, quick Ringgit-to-Gram currency conversion, and instant buy/sell asset updates.
* **Installment Buyers (EPP Users):** Require visual payment progress tracking, automated payment schedules, and clear installment due date notifications.
* **Physical Bullion Shoppers:** Require streamlined catalog browsing, transparent branch pickup locator maps, and secure delivery tracking options.
* **Platform Administrators:** Benefit from automated payment verification, reducing manual receipt slip verification workloads.

### Project Scope
* **In-Scope:** Heuristic evaluation, fishbone root-cause mapping, Information Architecture (IA) restructuring, high-fidelity Figma web/mobile wireframes, 3-step checkout workflow design, and System Usability Scale (SUS) evaluation planning.
* **Out-of-Scope:** Full-stack backend database engineering, live banking payment gateway API deployment, and production server hosting.
